Enable "Open Folder" on iOS via native bridge

When running inside the iOS wrapper (detected via the `__codeServerBridge`
injected by bridge.js), route the Open Folder command through the native
document picker rather than throwing. The bridge call returns a root id
and display name; we construct an `ipadfs:/<id>/` URI and open it via
the host service — the same path the simplified dialog uses.

The `OpenFolderWorkspaceSupportContext` context key (which hides the
Open Folder toolbar button and menu item) is extended to also be true
when the iOS bridge is available, so the affordance appears in the UI.

This patch follows the same pattern as code-server's
external-file-actions.diff: a construction-option-free runtime detection
via platform.ts helpers plus window-level bridge probing.

